  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Nursing, Vocational Certificate' program map, Catalog 2025-26, published July 21, 2025 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/6929/PublishedPdf). This is a Certificate of Achievement. Official Total Units: 54-55 = 18+12+12+12 = 54 at the low end, verified against the map's 18-19 / 12 / 12 / 12 headers. Semester 1 lists admission prerequisite courses that must be completed before applying to the LVN program; they are categorized as core here since they are required by the certificate path. The modeled path uses the first-listed options at the low end of variable units: ENGL C1000 at 3 units; BIOL 100 (3 units) rather than the BIOL 430 & 431 combination (documented alternative); PSYC 370 rather than EDUC 300; NUTRI 300 rather than NUTRI 480; PSYC C1000 rather than PSYC 480. In-plan prereqs sequenced: VN 130 requires VN 120 with a grade of C or better; VN 140 requires VN 130 with a grade of C or better. Enrollment criteria (documented, not all modeled in-plan): students must have BIOL 100 or BIOL 430 and 431 with a grade of B or better, and a cumulative GPA of 2.5 in AH 311; EDUC 300 or PSYC 370; NUTRI 300 or 480; ENGL C1000, ESLW 340, or ENGWR 488; and PSYC 300 or 480, passing each course with a C or better. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
